 external versions remain unresolved.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u31"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"Both readings concern one offered benefit in distribution of SFC-authorised funds. The actor is an intermediary distributing those funds. Product or product-type promotion includes linkage to funds of certain fund houses; online delivery, public advertising, a guarantee and demonstrated distraction are not express prerequisites. The broader reach of the underlying Code beyond this circular is unresolved.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u5","u14","u29"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Gift classification and genuine fee-discount classification require separate judgments. 'May be considered a gift' does not make all additional returns gifts. Actual fund return, distributor top-up and promoted service return are distinct. Neither 'gift' nor 'discount' receives an exhaustive definition here.","source_unit_ids":["u8","u13","u14","u21"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The express discount exception attaches to gifts. The rival question is whether product linkage limits only the promotion being assessed or also the fees eligible for discount. Section 103 authorisation/exemptions and dealing-procedure flexibility do not attach to this gift rule.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u14","u19"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The selected rule says 'should not', described as a requirement. The Boolean result identifies conduct caught by that restriction; it does not establish a statutory offence or complete compliance. Possible gift classification and discretionary regulatory action remain distinct from the restriction itself.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u13","u14","u15","u24"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"30 September 2010 identifies issuance of the cited FAQ, not commencement of this circular or the selected restriction. No applicable assessment-period rule is supplied. The synthetic snapshot date supplies no legal effective date, and guidance issued 'from time to time' requires version identification.","source_unit_ids":["u24","u30","u31"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"external-authorities.23ec46 is missing. The full Code paragraph 3.11 and FAQ answer could resolve classification, scope and exception breadth. Section 103, disclosure principles and advertising guidance are separate dependencies; the retained summary cannot establish their complete conditions.","source_unit_ids":["u7","u10","u12","u14","u22","u28","u29","u30","u31"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does the applicable full text of paragraph 3.11 or FAQ question 1 expressly limit the discount exception to fees relating to the promoted product?","What criteria distinguish a genuine fee discount from a cash gift or distributor-funded top-up, particularly for account-wide rebates?","Which versions of the Code and FAQ apply at the assessment date, and when did the relevant provisions take effect?","What formulas and fact bindings underlie the diagnostic node pairs? Their status labels alone cannot establish the substantive cause of disagreement or equivalence."],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The assessment concerns one offered benefit in a distributor’s promotion of SFC-authorised funds.","A genuine discount can be treated as excepted even where it otherwise falls within the assessed gift category.","Product-promotion linkage determines the scope of the restriction but does not add an unstated limitation to the fees eligible for discount.","Unknown classifications remain unknown; the result is evaluated only within the stated scope."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"Paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct provides that distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"u15"},{"quote":"2 The Code of Conduct for Persons Licensed by or Registered with the Securities and Futures Commission (Code of Conduct).","unit_id":"u29"}],"distinction":"This reading separates the promotional connection of the benefit from the subject matter of the discounted fees. A genuine discount of unrelated service fees is excepted even when offered to promote a fund. It has the stronger express wording because the parenthetical contains no product-related qualifier. Its strongest uncertainty is whether the missing Code or FAQ narrows what counts as an eligible discount. In the supplied snapshots, scope is true and gift_offered is true, but is_fee_discount remains unknown: this reading's result remains unknown. The parent reading yields true because discount_relates_to_promoted_product is false. This explains a possible difference without treating unknown as false or identifying undisclosed node formulas.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds in the assessed activity.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit is offered to a client in promotion of a specific fund or particular fund type, including a linkage to funds of certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit is offered and qualifies as a gift before applying the fee-discount exception; an additional return is not automatically classified as a gift.","name":"gift_offered","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit genuinely constitutes a discount of fees or charges, irrespective of which service those fees concern.","name":"is_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The fees or charges discounted by the assessed benefit relate to the promoted investment product or product type.","name":"discount_relates_to_promoted_product","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and gift_offered (not is_fee_discount))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor has_product_promotion_connection)"},"local_id":"r1","questions":["Does the unqualified wording of the exception extend to discounts on unrelated services or platform-wide fees?","Can the benefit be classified as a genuine discount independently of the marketing label used for it?"],"statement":"Selected control: paragraph-10 gift-promotion restriction with an unqualified fee-discount exception. Within scope, an offered gift is caught unless it genuinely constitutes a discount of fees or charges. The fees need not themselves relate to the promoted product. A true result identifies conduct caught by this selected restriction only.","subject":"Separating promotion scope from the definition of an excepted discount"},{"assumptions":["The assessment concerns one offered benefit in a distributor’s promotion of SFC-authorised funds.","A genuine discount can be treated as excepted even where it otherwise falls within the assessed gift category.","The surrounding product-promotion language implicitly confines the discount exception to fees or charges relating to that product; this qualification is not express.","Unknown classifications remain unknown; the result is evaluated only within the stated scope."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"other than a discount of fees or charges","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"The purpose of the requirement is to avoid the use of gifts to distract investors from the features and risks of a particular product.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement as investors may be distracted from the unique features and risks of such particular funds3.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"3 The answer to question 1 of the frequently asked questions on the Code of Conduct issued by the SFC on 30 September 2010.","unit_id":"u30"}],"distinction":"This retains the parent's contextual alternative: an unrelated-service discount remains caught when it is a gift connected with fund promotion. The anti-distraction purpose supports considering such benefits, but does not expressly narrow the parenthetical exception; that is the strongest weakness. With the supplied known gift and promotion facts and false product-relatedness, the result is true regardless of the unknown discount classification. A decisive fully known separation would require a genuine discount of unrelated fees: r1 would return false and r2 true. That is a conditional comparison, not an invented finding. The hypotheses that every additional return is automatically a gift, or that only public, online or guaranteed-return promotions qualify, are not supported by u13–u15. Incomparable bindings do not rebut either interpretation; equivalence within an undisclosed domain does not resolve this textual issue.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds in the assessed activity.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit is offered to a client in promotion of a specific fund or particular fund type, including a linkage to funds of certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit is offered and qualifies as a gift before applying the fee-discount exception; an additional return is not automatically classified as a gift.","name":"gift_offered","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit genuinely constitutes a discount of fees or charges, irrespective of which service those fees concern.","name":"is_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The fees or charges discounted by the assessed benefit relate to the promoted investment product or product type.","name":"discount_relates_to_promoted_product","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and gift_offered (not (and is_fee_discount discount_relates_to_promoted_product)))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor has_product_promotion_connection)"},"local_id":"r2","questions":["Does the full Code or FAQ supply the product-related limitation that this contextual reading implies?","Would account-level or platform-wide fee discounts count as relating to the promoted product?"],"statement":"Selected control: paragraph-10 gift-promotion restriction with a product-related fee-discount exception. Within scope, an offered gift is caught unless it genuinely discounts fees or charges relating to the promoted product or product type. A true result identifies conduct caught by this selected restriction only.","subject":"Contextual limitation on eligible discounted fees"}]}},"run_id":"run.d6106e5450c749a58852e36e6f81a6e0"}